---
title: Steamed Eggplant with Garlic (Syun Yeung Cing Keng Zi 蔥蒸茄子)
description: Soft steamed eggplant with a sizzling aromatic oil finish. Silky eggplant draped in savory-sweet sauce.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - eggplant
  - vegetarian
  - steamed
  - chinese
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/steamed-eggplant
cuisine: Chinese
course: Main
---

== Steam the Eggplant ==
Place the @long Asian eggplants{400%g} (cut into 5 cm batons) on a #heat-proof plate{}. Steam over boiling water in a #steamer{} for ~{10%minutes} until completely tender.

== Dress the Eggplant ==
-- The warm water helps dissolve the sugar before pouring
Mix the sauce: @light soy sauce{30%g}, @sugar{4%g}, @toasted sesame oil{2%g}, and @warm water{15%g}.
Carefully remove the plate from the steamer. Pour the mixed sauce over the eggplant.
Pile the @minced garlic{4%cloves}, @chopped scallion{1}, and @diced red chili{1} directly on top of the eggplant.

== Sizzling Oil Finish ==
-- The hot oil takes away the raw bite of the garlic and releases its fragrance
In a #small saucepan{}, heat the @neutral oil{28%g} until it is smoking hot. Carefully pour the hot oil directly over the garlic and scallion pile to sizzle.
